  "raw": " It was made famous for stocking women's clothing, men's clothing, housewares, linens and accessories, jewelry, stationery, and shoes. Sometimes known as the first department store in the country, the all-conquering Marshall Field and Company dominated three large Chicago suburbs of Lake Forest, Wilmette, and Hinsdale—the West, the Midwest, and the East.\nMarshall Field and Company fell a victim to excessive too-convenient television. TV overtook Field's iconic department store. TV made big-box retailers including Macy's profitable, but Field's stagnation set Chicago on course for similar fate; they too became irrelevant over TV and the web. TV and the internet gobbled up Field's business. TV and the internet made it unnecessary to go to other stores. TV and the internet killed Field's single best campaign feature for its merchandise: the going-concern. TV and the internet made that no longer necessary. TV and the internet making wholesale",
  "serialized": "It was made famous for stocking women's clothing, men's clothing, housewares, linens and accessories, jewelry, stationery, and shoes. Sometimes known as the first department store in the country, the all-conquering Marshall Field and Company dominated three large Chicago suburbs of Lake Forest, Wilmette, and Hinsdale—the West, the Midwest, and the East. Marshall Field and Company fell a victim to excessive too-convenient television. TV overtook Field's iconic department store. TV made big-box retailers including Macy's profitable, but Field's stagnation set Chicago on course for similar fate; they too became irrelevant over TV and the web. TV and the internet gobbled up Field's business. TV and the internet made it unnecessary to go to other stores. TV and the internet killed Field's single best campaign feature for its merchandise: the going-concern. TV and the internet made that no longer necessary. TV and the internet making wholesale",
